# `local.rs`'s `no_failure_prefix_is_a_prefix_of_another` is NOT the precedent for
# a hand-written list of copies. Its own comment says it "names the consts rather
# than the strings, so it cannot drift from the wire" - hand-written *references*
# to one source of truth. A doc comment cannot be referenced from Python, so the
# copy is unavoidable here; what was avoidable is leaving it unchecked.
#
# ── the haystack is BACKTICKED SPANS IN COMMENTS, and both narrowings were bugs
#
# A first version searched the whole of `lives_in`, and that made this check a
# TAUTOLOGY for every same-file row: `lives_in == target`, so the CODE LINE
