# Distinct, because the haystack below is a `set`. By OCCURRENCE the same measurement
# reads 6 and 2, since two records quote that anchor. Every other figure in this file
# is an occurrence count, so the unit is named here rather than inferred - a
# re-measurer who gets 6 and 2, disagrees, and re-derives is the failure the
# DESCRIBED header warns about.
#
# **Not by comparing indentation, which cannot work here.** The obvious reading -
# "the record's span must equal the literal including its leading whitespace" -
# reddens most of this list. Records quote UNINDENTED on purpose: that is the whole
# mechanism leaving the indented literal unique in the target (mode 1), so a rule
# built on the exceptions breaks the convention.
#
# **Both figures this paragraph used to carry went stale, and one of them changed
# sides.** It said the rule "reddens 9 of the 19 rows" and that "only C8's record
# quotes its anchor with the indentation". Re-measured at `080fec7`, over the rows
# whose REGISTERED literal carries indentation, comparing each record's flat-matching
# span: **C8, C13, P1 and P2** keep the whitespace, and thirty rows drop it. C8 is
# still one of the four and is no longer alone, so a rule derived from "that one row"
# would now be derived from four. **`P1` and `P2` are the registry's ONLY `P` rows and
# BOTH of them keep the whitespace** - `parked-drain` did not contribute one of these
# four, it contributed every row it owns, which is the fact a per-branch count of one
# hid.
# The conclusion did not move, which is the trap: a paragraph whose numbers are stale
# and whose point is sound reads as already checked.
#
# Lines are joined BEFORE the spans are cut out, so a quote the comment wrapped
# across two `///` lines is still one span - and `comment_blocks` is what joins
# them, the same reader the population walk goes through. This check owning a
# private reader is exactly how the two came to disagree.
def quoted_spans(path: str) -> set[str]:
    """Every backticked span inside a comment of `path`, whitespace-flattened."""
    return set().union(*(spans(b) for b in comment_blocks((ROOT / path).read_text())))


